  "report_period": "Week 15 (3rd Apr to 9th Apr 2026)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "The Post Panamax \"Yangze 901\" 93/2012 Jiangsu, China (SS/DD 01/2027) was committed to Chinese interests at USD 12,8 mill. For comparison, the one-year-older sister vessel \"Welfine\" 93/2011 Jiangsu, China (SS/DD 05/2026) was sold a month ago at USD 11,8 mill. Navios Maritime committed their Panamax \"N Amalthia\" 75/2006 Universal, Japan (SS/DD 11/2026) to undisclosed interests at USD 10,3 mill. Note that the one-year-older \"Ocean Lion\" 76/2005 Sanoyas, Japan (SS 10/2030, DD 10/2028) was sold a month ago at USD 10 mill. On the Supramax sector, Ningbo Zrich Shipping committed the \"Petrus\" 57/2011 Stx, Korea (SS/DD 04/2026) at high USD 13 mill, while the one-year- older sister vessel \"Serene Amelia\" 57/2010 Stx, Korea (SS 09/2029, DD 12/2027) of Century Bulk Carriers was sold at mid USD 14 mill. For reference, the \"Platon\" 58/2011 Spp, Korea (SS/DD 08/2026) was committed a week ago at USD 15,4 mill. The Handysize \"Nanaimo Bay\" 34/2016 Namura & Sasebo, Japan (SS/DD 12/2026) was committed at excess USD 19 mill basis delivery June-August 2026. Remind you that back in February, the two-years-older sister vessels \"African Dove\" & \"African Lark\" 34/2014 Namura & Sasebo, Japan (SS 05/2029, DD 09/2027 & SS 04/2029, DD 04/2027) were sold at USD 16,5 mill each. In addition, the \"Cosco Kunlunshan\" 31/2010 Fujian Mawei, China (SS 07/2030, DD 06/2028) & \"Jin Wang Ling\" 31/2010 Guangzhou, China (SS 01/2030, DD 01/2028) were committed at USD 8,2 mill each. For comparison, the \"Sea Sapphire\" 32/2010 Zhejiang, China (SS 03/2030, DD 05/2028) was sold in March at USD 8,5 mill.",
    "tankers": "Eastwind Marine Services have committed the LR1 \"Ever Victory\" 70/2005 Universal, Japan (SS 06/2030, DD 07/2028) to undisclosed interests at USD 14,7 mill. For reference, the one-year-younger \"PGC Alexandria\" 75/2006 Onomichi, Japan (SS 10/2029, DD 10/2027) was sold back in February at USD 15,75 mill. The MR2 \"Ocean Spirit\" 50/2012 Spp, Korea (SS/DD 10/2027) of OceanGold Tankers was committed at USD 27 mill. For comparison, the \"High Seas\" 50/2012 Hyundai Mipo, Korea (SS/DD 03/2027) was sold a couple of weeks ago at USD 27,6 mill.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "Iron ore rates on the West Australia / China route continued throughout",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "North Pacific rounds with redelivery in the Singapore-Japan range were reported between usd 15,000/17,000 pd. A number of Australian trips into South East Asia were fixed at levels ranging from usd 15,000/18,000 pd. China trips via Indonesia into China were reported around usd 12,000/15,000 pd. East Coast South American trips into Singapore-Japan range were fixed at usd 18,000/21,000 pd. Additionally, India trips via East Coast South America into Singapore-Japan were reported at usd 22,000 pd. West Mediterranean trips into Singapore-Japan were fixed around usd 23,000 pd. On the period front, Kamsarmaxes were reported fixed in the usd 19,000/20,000 pd range for 11/13 months employment.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "Indonesia trips into East Coast India ranged at the usd 15,000 pd level. A number of South Africa trips into India were reported at the level of usd 21,000/24,000 pd. US Gulf trips into Persian Gulf-Japan range were fixed around usd 19,000 pd. East Coast South American trips into North Coast South America were fixed in a range of usd 20,000 pd. Continent trips into the Mediterranean were reported around usd 17,000 pd.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "Trips from West Africa into the Mediterranean were fixed around usd 9,000 pd."
    }
  },
